<Description contentType="preformatted" classID="1EAB3E07-9C6F-4559-97B0-AC4253FEDDDC">
  <Abstract>&lt;Content&gt;The method &lt;code&gt;Boolean.getBoolean()&lt;/code&gt; is often confused with &lt;code&gt;Boolean.valueOf()&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;Boolean.parseBoolean()&lt;/code&gt; method calls.&lt;/Content&gt;</Abstract>
  <Explanation>&lt;Content&gt;In most cases, a call to &lt;code&gt;Boolean.getBoolean()&lt;/code&gt; is often misused as it is assumed to return the boolean value represented by the specified string argument. However, as stated in the Javadoc &lt;code&gt;Boolean.getBoolean(String)&lt;/code&gt; method "Returns true if and only if the system property named by the argument exists and is equal to the string 'true'."

Most often what the developer intended to use was a call to &lt;code&gt;Boolean.valueOf(String)&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;Boolean.parseBoolean(String)&lt;/code&gt; method.
&lt;b&gt;Example 1:&lt;/b&gt; The following code will not behave as expected. It will print "FALSE" as &lt;code&gt;Boolean.getBoolean(String)&lt;/code&gt; does not translate a String primitive. It only translates system property.
&lt;pre&gt;
 ...
 String isValid = "true";
 if ( Boolean.getBoolean(isValid) ) {
     System.out.println("TRUE");
 }
 else {
     System.out.println("FALSE");
 }
 ...
&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/Content&gt;</Explanation>
  <Recommendations>&lt;Content&gt;Please ensure that you intend to call the method &lt;code&gt;Boolean.getBoolean(String)&lt;/code&gt; and the specified string argument is a system property. Else the method call you are most likely looking for is &lt;code&gt;Boolean.valueOf(String)&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;Boolean.parseBoolean(String)&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/Content&gt;</Recommendations>
  <References>
    <Reference>
      <Title>Class Boolean</Title>
      <Publisher>Oracle</Publisher>
      <Source>http://docs.oracle.com/javase/6/docs/api/java/lang/Boolean.html</Source>
    </Reference>
    <Reference>
      <Title>Requirement 6.5.6</Title>
      <Author>Standards Mapping - Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard Version 3.0</Author>
    </Reference>
    <Reference>
      <Title>Requirement 6.5.6</Title>
      <Author>Standards Mapping - Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard Version 3.1</Author>
    </Reference>
    <Reference>
      <Title>Requirement 6.5.6</Title>
      <Author>Standards Mapping - Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard Version 3.2</Author>
    </Reference>
    <Reference>
      <Title>Requirement 6.5.6</Title>
      <Author>Standards Mapping - Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard Version 3.2.1</Author>
    </Reference>
